    "body": "It's not a small amount of work but I think taking this one step at a time is best and perhaps others will start helping, as well. The first step will be getting raytracing working on WebGPU compute shaders in a simple case. Something like this [three-mesh-bvh normals path tracing example](https://gkjohnson.github.io/three-mesh-bvh/example/bundle/gpuPathTracingSimple.html) or [this lambert one](https://gkjohnson.github.io/three-mesh-bvh/example/bundle/gpuPathTracing.html) but with compute shaders. Once that's prepared we can start looking into adding a new WebGPU path tracer in this project and work up to all the same features in the WebGL version.\r\n\r\nIf you're looking for more references on path tracing in general I can recommend Peter Shirley's [Raytracing in One Weekend](https://raytracing.github.io/) online book series. And the [PBR Book](https://www.pbr-book.org/) for more advanced concepts.",
